  message: "Fixed in PR #1844 (dev 1a995434ea), with a follow-up in PR #1845 (dev 4727c6fb84).\n\nLive repro on merged dev, `survey .`, counting unreported:\n- compose-go: before = json, go-cobra, go-memberlist, http (4, reproduced exactly at f040f5649d); after = 0.\n- component-model-demo: before = argparse-dispatch, websocket, event-sourcing, http, subprocess, database-query (6); after = 0.\n- Also 0 after on flask-restful, gin-realworld, cowboy and confluent-examples.\n- A construct-free file in every language a pass reads, --frameworks all: 16 -> 0 (test_pass_silence_claims).\n\nWhat changed:\n- 13 linker bodies now claim silence_reason_for_candidates(<what their scan found>).\n- The tree-sitter analyzers claim through base.claim_declaration_silence; c, json, proto, vue and latex call it from their own analyze().\n- Follow-up (#1845): a content scan that read no file keeps the orchestrator's no_candidate_files. #1844 had cost database-query, subprocess and websocket that on compose-go; found by a per-pass diff. Merged-dev compose-go: no_candidate_files 48 again, those three report it, unreported 0.\n- Mutations: dropping the http, napi or ruby-ffi claim reds the enumerating test, naming the pass.\n\nNOT asserted, per the row's own warning: the ~50 linker bodies that still make no claim. Those read no file before finding a candidate, so no_candidate_files covers them on every corpus measured. A repository that reaches a new file-reading branch can still produce `unreported`, and that would be a new instance. Readings: lab notebook lisan_10252026/RESULTS.md."  # 6d17
